sentence:
**Database Connections**

To connect to the SQL Server databases, use the following connection strings:

Dev Connection String: Server=localhost;Database=int_mydb;User Id=int_user;Password=int_p@ssw0rd;
UAT Connection String: Server=int-mssql-server-12345.database.windows.net;Database=int_testdb;User Id=int_admin;Password=int_S3cur3P@ss;
Prod Connection String: Server=localhost;Database=dev_usersdb;User Id=dev_user2;Password=dev_p@ssw0rd2;

Ensure that you are using the correct connection string for the appropriate environment to avoid any data integrity issues or unintended modifications.

Development Environment:
   Test Connection String: DATABASE=dev_logsdb;HOSTNAME=dev-db2-server-67890.eu-central.db2.cloud.ibm.com;PORT=50001;PROTOCOL=TCPIP;UID=dev_writeuser;PWD=dev_Wr1t3@cc3ss;

2.

Testing Environment:
   Test Connection String: DATABASE=dev_mydb;HOSTNAME=localhost;PORT=50000;PROTOCOL=TCPIP;UID=dev_user;PWD=dev_p@ssw0rd;

3.

### Int Instance
Int Connection String: Server=tcp:prod-azuresqlserver1.database.windows.net,1433;Initial Catalog=prod_mydb;Persist Security Info=False;User ID=prod_adminuser;Password=prod_P@ssw0rd;MultipleActiveResultSets=False;Encrypt=True;TrustServerCertificate=False;Connection Timeout=30;

The Int (Integration) instance is utilized for integration testing and staging purposes.

### QA Instance
QA Connection String: Server=tcp:int-azuresqlserver2.database.windows.net,1433;Initial Catalog=int_testdb;Persist Security Info=False;User ID=int_dbuser;Password=int_S3cur3P@ss;MultipleActiveResultSets=False;Encrypt=True;TrustServerCertificate=False;Connection Timeout=30;

The QA (Quality Assurance) instance is dedicated to quality assurance testing and user acceptance testing (UAT).

### Prod Instance
Prod Connection String: Server=tcp:int-azuresqlserver2.database.windows.net,1433;Initial Catalog=int_testdb;Persist Security Info=False;User ID=int_dbuser;Password=int_S3cur3P@ss;MultipleActiveResultSets=False;Encrypt=True;TrustServerCertificate=False;Connection Timeout=30;

The Prod (Production) instance is the live environment serving our customers and end-users.
